data_SnSe_orthorhombic_Pnma
# Orthorhombic SnSe (Pnma, space group 62), 8-atom primitive cell (= conv).
# Lattice parameters a = 11.498 Å, b = 4.151 Å, c = 4.445 Å (room T).
# This is the low-temperature alpha phase. The high-T beta phase (Cmcm)
# above ~800 K is what gives SnSe its record-breaking ZT of ~2.6 along
# the b axis.
# Wyckoff 4c sites for Sn and Se with x_Sn ≈ 0.119, z_Sn ≈ 0.108
# and x_Se ≈ 0.151, z_Se ≈ 0.481 (approximate room-T positions).
#
# Sources:
#   - Zhao, L.-D. et al. "Ultralow thermal conductivity and high
#     thermoelectric figure of merit in SnSe crystals", Nature 508,
#     373–377 (2014). DOI: 10.1038/nature13184
#   - Chattopadhyay, T. et al. "Neutron and X-ray diffraction studies of
#     the structural phase transition in SnSe", J. Phys. Chem. Solids
#     47(9), 879–885 (1986). DOI: 10.1016/0022-3697(86)90059-4
#   - Materials Project entry mp-691 (SnSe Pnma).
_cell_length_a 11.498
_cell_length_b 4.151
_cell_length_c 4.445
_cell_angle_alpha 90.0
_cell_angle_beta 90.0
_cell_angle_gamma 90.0
_symmetry_space_group_name_H-M 'P 1'
_symmetry_Int_Tables_number 1
